1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,920
You  already  know  that  identity

2
00:00:01,920 --> 00:00:04,200
describes  who  you  are.  Now  we

3
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:05,279
need  to  make  that  knowledge

4
00:00:05,279 --> 00:00:07,600
useful.  Self-awareness  means

5
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:09,240
recognizing  your  strengths,

6
00:00:09,240 --> 00:00:12,280
weaknesses,  abilities,  habits,  and

7
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:13,960
the  way  you  usually  respond  to

8
00:00:13,960 --> 00:00:15,759
situations.  In  the  source

9
00:00:15,759 --> 00:00:17,760
curriculum,  this  matters  because  a

10
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:19,760
person  who  understands  themselves

11
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:21,000
can  make  better  use  of  their

12
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:22,400
strengths  and  work  more

13
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:24,519
deliberately  on  their  weaknesses.

14
00:00:24,519 --> 00:00:26,320
For  a  community  leader,  that  is

15
00:00:26,320 --> 00:00:28,400
essential.  Leadership  does  not

16
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:30,000
begin  with  controlling  other  people

17
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,239
people.  It  begins  with  understanding

18
00:00:32,239 --> 00:00:34,280
what  you  can  contribute,  where  you

19
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:36,079
still  need  to  grow  and  how  your

20
00:00:36,079 --> 00:00:37,960
behavior  affects  the  people  around

21
00:00:37,960 --> 00:00:38,416
you.

22
00:00:38,696 --> 00:00:40,736
Not  every  ability  develops  in  the

23
00:00:40,736 --> 00:00:43,215
same  way.  Some  strengths  may  come

24
00:00:43,215 --> 00:00:45,416
naturally  to  you,  while  others  are

25
00:00:45,416 --> 00:00:48,055
built  through  effort  and  practice.

26
00:00:48,055 --> 00:00:49,736
The  important  point  is  not  whether

27
00:00:49,736 --> 00:00:52,496
a  skill  was  given  or  learned.

28
00:00:52,496 --> 00:00:54,255
The  important  point  is  whether  you

29
00:00:54,255 --> 00:00:56,896
recognize  it  and  develop  it.

30
00:00:56,896 --> 00:00:59,216
At  the  same  time,  no  person  has

31
00:00:59,216 --> 00:01:02,136
every  skill  a  real  project  needs.

32
00:01:02,136 --> 00:01:03,615
One  person  may  be  strong  at

33
00:01:03,615 --> 00:01:06,256
organizing,  another  at  listening,

34
00:01:06,256 --> 00:01:08,535
another  at  solving  problems.  And

35
00:01:08,535 --> 00:01:10,736
another  at  communicating.

36
00:01:10,736 --> 00:01:12,616
Self-awareness  helps  you  stop

37
00:01:12,616 --> 00:01:14,655
pretending  you  must  do  everything

38
00:01:14,655 --> 00:01:17,016
yourself  and  start  understanding

39
00:01:17,016 --> 00:01:18,536
where  other  people's  strengths

40
00:01:18,536 --> 00:01:19,749
complete  your  own.

41
00:01:19,749 --> 00:01:22,309
Let's  make  this  personal.  Complete

42
00:01:22,309 --> 00:01:24,349
these  six  sentence  starters.

43
00:01:24,349 --> 00:01:28,428
I  can,  I  enjoy,  I  believe  in,  I

44
00:01:28,428 --> 00:01:31,069
spend  my  time  in,  I  am  learning

45
00:01:31,069 --> 00:01:34,548
to  and  I  feel  when.

46
00:01:34,548 --> 00:01:36,189
Pause  the  video  and  finish  all

47
00:01:36,189 --> 00:01:38,589
six  honestly  either  out  loud  or

48
00:01:38,589 --> 00:01:41,149
in  writing.

49
00:01:41,429 --> 00:01:42,989
When  you  come  back,  look  at  the

50
00:01:42,989 --> 00:01:45,028
pattern  in  your  answers.  What  do

51
00:01:45,028 --> 00:01:46,069
they  tell  you  about  your

52
00:01:46,069 --> 00:01:48,469
abilities,  interests,  values  and

53
00:01:48,469 --> 00:01:49,788
habits?

54
00:01:49,788 --> 00:01:51,469
This  is  the  real  purpose  of  the

55
00:01:51,469 --> 00:01:53,669
activity.  Not  to  create  perfect

56
00:01:53,669 --> 00:01:55,789
sentences,  but  to  help  you  notice

57
00:01:55,789 --> 00:01:57,828
specific  things  about  yourself  that

58
00:01:57,828 --> 00:01:59,229
can  shape  the  way  you  contribute

59
00:01:59,229 --> 00:02:01,415
to  a  team  and  to  your  community.

60
00:02:01,415 --> 00:02:03,014
This  leads  to  one  of  the  most

61
00:02:03,014 --> 00:02:05,535
important  ideas  in  the  lesson.  A

62
00:02:05,535 --> 00:02:07,774
strong  team  is  not  a  group  of

63
00:02:07,774 --> 00:02:09,974
identical  people.  It  is  a  group

64
00:02:09,974 --> 00:02:11,495
where  different  abilities  are

65
00:02:11,495 --> 00:02:13,735
understood  and  combined.

66
00:02:13,735 --> 00:02:15,295
The  source  curriculum  makes  this

67
00:02:15,295 --> 00:02:17,014
clear  through  examples  such  as  a

68
00:02:17,014 --> 00:02:19,614
school  or  a  construction  project.

69
00:02:19,614 --> 00:02:22,015
One  person  cannot  perform  every

70
00:02:22,015 --> 00:02:23,575
role  alone.

71
00:02:23,575 --> 00:02:25,335
A  project  becomes  stronger  when

72
00:02:25,335 --> 00:02:27,175
people  know  what  they  are  good  at

73
00:02:27,175 --> 00:02:28,694
and  trust  others  with  different

74
00:02:28,694 --> 00:02:30,335
responsibilities.

75
00:02:30,335 --> 00:02:32,375
For  a  community  leader  This  means

76
00:02:32,375 --> 00:02:34,415
leadership  is  not  proving  that  you

77
00:02:34,415 --> 00:02:36,695
can  do  everything.  It  is  helping

78
00:02:36,695 --> 00:02:38,134
people  use  their  different

79
00:02:38,134 --> 00:02:40,831
strengths  toward  one  shared  result.

80
00:02:40,831 --> 00:02:42,990
The  rabbit  and  turtle  example  in

81
00:02:42,990 --> 00:02:44,991
the  curriculum  shows  this  idea  in

82
00:02:44,991 --> 00:02:47,630
a  simple  way.  Pause  the  video  and

83
00:02:47,630 --> 00:02:49,711
watch  the  linked  clip.

84
00:02:49,711 --> 00:02:51,631
As  you  watch,  focus  on  the

85
00:02:51,631 --> 00:02:53,751
abilities  of  each  character,  not

86
00:02:53,751 --> 00:02:56,630
only  on  who  wins.  Ask  yourself,

87
00:02:56,630 --> 00:02:58,711
what  can  the  rabbit  do  well?  What

88
00:02:58,711 --> 00:03:00,431
can  the  turtle  do  well?

89
00:03:00,431 --> 00:03:02,231
What  changes  when  they  understand

90
00:03:02,231 --> 00:03:04,671
their  own  strengths  and  weaknesses?

91
00:03:04,671 --> 00:03:06,430
And  what  becomes  possible  when

92
00:03:06,430 --> 00:03:08,471
they  cooperate  instead  of  treating

93
00:03:08,471 --> 00:03:11,311
every  situation  as  a  competition?

94
00:03:11,311 --> 00:03:13,230
When  you  return,  remember  the

95
00:03:13,230 --> 00:03:15,511
lesson  behind  the  story.  Different

96
00:03:15,511 --> 00:03:17,910
abilities  are  not  a  problem.  They

97
00:03:17,910 --> 00:03:19,390
become  useful  when  people

98
00:03:19,390 --> 00:03:21,539
understand  how  to  combine  them.

99
00:03:21,859 --> 00:03:23,938
Self-awareness  also  changes  the  way

100
00:03:23,938 --> 00:03:26,298
you  understand  other  people.

101
00:03:26,298 --> 00:03:27,818
Once  you  begin  noticing  your  own

102
00:03:27,818 --> 00:03:30,859
habits,  emotions  and  needs,  other

103
00:03:30,859 --> 00:03:32,699
people's  behavior  can  become  easier

104
00:03:32,699 --> 00:03:34,178
to  interpret.

105
00:03:34,178 --> 00:03:35,739
Someone  may  react  differently  from

106
00:03:35,739 --> 00:03:37,699
you  because  their  priorities,

107
00:03:37,699 --> 00:03:39,939
personality  or  way  of  working  is

108
00:03:39,939 --> 00:03:41,019
different.

109
00:03:41,019 --> 00:03:42,499
That  does  not  automatically  make

110
00:03:42,499 --> 00:03:44,658
them  difficult  or  wrong.

111
00:03:44,658 --> 00:03:46,179
The  source  curriculum  connects

112
00:03:46,179 --> 00:03:48,099
knowing  yourself  with  being  more

113
00:03:48,099 --> 00:03:50,019
aware  of  others  because

114
00:03:50,019 --> 00:03:51,859
understanding  your  own  pattern

115
00:03:51,859 --> 00:03:53,579
helps  you  accept  that  other  people

116
00:03:53,579 --> 00:03:55,418
have  patterns  too.

117
00:03:55,418 --> 00:03:57,098
This  is  where  self-awareness  begins

118
00:03:57,098 --> 00:03:58,899
to  move  outward  and  become  a

119
00:03:58,899 --> 00:04:01,080
foundation  for  cooperation.

120
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:03,479
The  bridge  video  develops  this  idea

121
00:04:03,479 --> 00:04:05,839
through  conflict.  Pause  the  video

122
00:04:05,839 --> 00:04:07,919
and  watch  the  linked  clip.

123
00:04:07,919 --> 00:04:09,599
Notice  why  the  first  characters

124
00:04:09,599 --> 00:04:11,360
fail,  what  their  selfishness

125
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:13,080
creates  and  what  the  later

126
00:04:13,080 --> 00:04:15,120
characters  do  differently.

127
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:16,320
The  lesson  is  not  that

128
00:04:16,320 --> 00:04:18,480
disagreement  should  disappear.

129
00:04:18,480 --> 00:04:19,800
It  is  that  a  leader  must  know

130
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:22,160
how  to  manage  disagreement  without

131
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:24,199
letting  it  damage  the  group.

132
00:04:24,199 --> 00:04:26,080
A  successful  leader  listens,

133
00:04:26,080 --> 00:04:27,480
understands  different  points  of

134
00:04:27,480 --> 00:04:29,519
view  and  helps  people  find  a  way

135
00:04:29,519 --> 00:04:30,880
forward.

136
00:04:30,880 --> 00:04:33,000
In  a  real  ACT  project,  team

137
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,360
members  may  disagree  about

138
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:37,319
priorities,  roles  or  solutions.

139
00:04:37,319 --> 00:04:39,240
Self-awareness  helps  you  respond  to

140
00:04:39,240 --> 00:04:41,080
that  conflict  instead  of  simply

141
00:04:41,080 --> 00:04:42,330
reacting  to  it.

142
00:04:42,729 --> 00:04:44,890
So,  what  did  you  really  learn

143
00:04:44,890 --> 00:04:46,130
today?

144
00:04:46,130 --> 00:04:48,410
Self-awareness  is  not  just  being

145
00:04:48,410 --> 00:04:50,810
able  to  describe  yourself.  It  is

146
00:04:50,810 --> 00:04:52,889
knowing  how  to  use  what  you

147
00:04:52,889 --> 00:04:55,290
understand  about  yourself.

148
00:04:55,290 --> 00:04:57,089
You  learned  that  strengths  should

149
00:04:57,089 --> 00:04:59,410
be  developed,  weaknesses  should  be

150
00:04:59,410 --> 00:05:02,369
worked  on  or  supported  by  others,

151
00:05:02,369 --> 00:05:04,650
different  abilities  make  teams

152
00:05:04,650 --> 00:05:07,730
stronger.  And  understanding  yourself

153
00:05:07,730 --> 00:05:10,009
helps  you  understand  and  work  with

154
00:05:10,009 --> 00:05:11,730
other  people.

155
00:05:11,730 --> 00:05:14,290
That  is  Why  self-awareness  matters

156
00:05:14,290 --> 00:05:16,490
to  a  community  leader.

157
00:05:16,490 --> 00:05:18,290
Keep  your  six  sentences  with  your

158
00:05:18,290 --> 00:05:20,170
personal  identity  wheel.

159
00:05:20,170 --> 00:05:21,729
They  are  becoming  a  picture  of

160
00:05:21,729 --> 00:05:24,010
what  you  bring  to  a  team.

161
00:05:24,010 --> 00:05:25,650
In  the  next  lesson,  we  move

162
00:05:25,650 --> 00:05:27,610
directly  into  leadership  and

163
00:05:27,610 --> 00:05:29,810
explore  what  leadership  actually

164
00:05:29,810 --> 00:05:30,788
means.

